Z||000001||rogergarrison||09-05-2001||06:46 AM||||Keep checking the forum. Try to find any car shows or cruise ins that are in your area. Dont have to be all Fiero show to have fun. I go to 1 or 2 every weekend almost.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||09-05-2001||07:32 AM||||This is too good to pass up!<P>You show me yours, I'll show you mine.<P>Seriously, just look around this board.  Fiero "official" clubs exist in Austin, San Antonio, Houston and even a North Texas Fiero Club.<P>Houston (Central Texas) is having a meet in Huntsville (Oct 20th, I think) and another meet is scheduled for North Texas (Southlake, near D/FW Airport), Oct 13th.<P>Come to any or all!<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Denny||09-05-2001||07:43 AM||||Here are the Fiero clubs located in Texas:<P>Austin Fiero Club: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/1994/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/1994/</A> <P>Lone Star Fieros: <A HREF="http://www.flash.net/~newboy/lonestar.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.flash.net/~newboy/lonestar.html</A> <P>Alamo Area Fiero Owners: <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/AlamoAreaFieroOwners/_whatsnew.msnw" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/AlamoAreaFieroOwners/_whatsnew.msnw</A> <P>North Texas Fiero Car Club: <A HREF="http://www.ntfc.org/index2.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ntfc.org/index2.htm</A> <P>I see that the Austin Fiero Club has a show scheduled for October 27.<P>You can also check bulletin boards at local drive-in restaurants for show info.<P>Finally, you can check with the Pontiac Oakland Club International (POCI) chapters in your state to find out where the all-pontiac shows are in your area.  Contacts in Texas are:<P>Lone Star Chapter (TX), c/o Joe Rakoczy, 7208 Tumbleweed Ct., Colleyville, TX 76034<P>So. Central Texas Chapter, c/o Jay Lord, P.0. Box 34654, San Antonio, TX 78265<P>Have fun!<P>||||reg||6
